# Mirrors the "hosting.ignore" list in firebase.json so both hosts serve the
# same set of files.
#
# IMPORTANT: game/ is deliberately absent from this list even though .gitignore
# excludes it. The Unity Web build is generated, not committed, and Vercel falls
# back to .gitignore when no .vercelignore exists -- without this file the deploy
# would ship the page with no player behind it.
#
# Related: vercel.json sets git.deploymentEnabled=false. A deployment built from
# the git repo cannot contain game/ at all, so it serves play.html with no player
# and 404s every /game/ path. Ship with `vercel deploy --prod` from the machine
# that has Unity, the same way Firebase Hosting is deployed.

.claude
.firebase
node_modules
firebase.json
database.rules.json
serve.py
unity
*.md
